# Cloudflare static-asset response headers (copied into dist/ by Vite).
#
# /love/* and /assets/* never change under a URL: Vite fingerprints
# /assets/ file names, and every /love/ reference carries its content hash as
# `?v=` (vite.config.ts, frontend/lua/build.mjs). Pages (index.html for every
# route) keep the platform default, `max-age=0, must-revalidate`, so a deploy
# shows up on the next load.
#
# Every response also gets the security headers below (security audit AE3);
# rules that match a path add up, and no header is set by two rules. The page's
# content policy stays the <meta> CSP that vite.config.ts writes; this header
# CSP only forbids framing, which a <meta> CSP cannot, and intersects with it.
# Permissions-Policy leaves clipboard-write, fullscreen and gamepad alone (the
# bridge copies decklists and invite links). No COEP: the love.js build is
# single-threaded and needs no cross-origin isolation. HSTS waits for a custom
# domain; the .dev TLD under workers.dev is HSTS-preloaded.

/*
  Content-Security-Policy: frame-ancestors 'none'
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=(), payment=(), usb=()
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin

# Compression comes from the Content-Type wrangler gives each file: Cloudflare compresses only
# the types it lists, and .data gets none, so the game package also ships as game.data.gz
# (application/gzip, sent as is), which host.js unpacks itself (frontend/lua/build.mjs).
/love/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/favicon.svg
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=86400, stale-while-revalidate=604800
